---
/**
 * Overrides Starlight's theme provider to pin the Docs to dark.
 *
 * Starlight's default reads localStorage, then falls back to
 * prefers-color-scheme. The Site has no light theme — site-tokens.css mirrors
 * the app's dark-theme pane palette byte-for-byte and Nocturne ships no light
 * ramp — so a visitor on a light-mode OS would otherwise get Starlight's light
 * defaults for everything the mapping in styles/starlight.css does not cover:
 * asides, code blocks, the note/tip/caution colour families.
 *
 * The `updatePickers` stub is kept because Starlight's own code calls it; the
 * picker itself is overridden away in components/ThemeSelect.astro.
 *
 * To bring light mode back, delete this file and its entry in
 * astro.config.mjs, and split the mappings in styles/starlight.css by
 * [data-theme].
 */
---

{/* Intentionally inlined to avoid a flash of the wrong theme. */}
<script is:inline>
  window.StarlightThemeProvider = (() => {
    document.documentElement.dataset.theme = 'dark';
    return { updatePickers() {} };
  })();
</script>
